    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - Chat03B2 operator credential lifecycle 0007\n\n**Exact HEAD reviewed:** `0e3f07e7b8a12aa9333e95ca251de84e65bdb9a5`, tree `eeffc764327bf080b50e0b4c57b992ae592f3e36`, immediate parent `801cfe86f809fbc8e6cd84350e028316c44639ee`. Existing [Draft PR446](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/pull/446) targets exact Draft PR445 HEAD `7cb5bc8a36f6c0c1ce36e88236a729be5ac9d036`: **2 ahead, 0 behind**, four expected files only (`0007_capability_operator_lifecycle.sql`, `src/worker.js`, `private_api_local_test.mjs`, `test_chat03b2_capability_operator_lifecycle_sql.py`). OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, mergeable clean. No merge, hosted or production changes.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS_NARROW_LOCAL_OPERATOR_CREDENTIAL_LIFECYCLE_0007` / NOT private-alpha release authorization.** Independently inspected migration, Worker routing and tests. Trusted admin Bearer `ADMIN_CONTROL_TOKEN` gates `POST /v1/admin/battles/{battleId}/capabilities/{A|B}/revoke|replace` with no browser Origin/preflight allowance. `revoke` atomically checks current status plus expected generation, records revoked and increments generation. `replace` generates fresh bearer server-side and atomically updates active status/new digest/+1 generation with SQL compare-and-update; only returns new bearer on successful mutation. SQL triggers constrain ordinary status/generation/digest transitions and identity changes and keep an append-only hash registry. Existing 0006 SQL capability mutation trigger closes any fresh creation recovery in the same transaction. SQL write fence and Worker scheduler isolation remain unchanged.\n\n**Exact-head GitHub Actions independently verified from run metadata, jobs and actual logs:** [Private API #40457090075](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090075) SUCCESS, local isolated workerd/D1 actually applies `0001-0007` and tests revoke, replace, old A rejection/new A acceptance, unchanged B, restart, race duplicate replace/revoke-vs-replace, lost response operator repair, old replay and AES failures; [CAS SQL #40457090267](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090267) SUCCESS with **61/61** Python discovery and two new lifecycle SQL tests; [AI Forensics #40457090102](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40457090102) SUCCESS. All exact HEAD `0e3f07e...`, completed attempt 1. Codex local repository policy/syntax/diff checks reported, not independently rerun.\n\n**Security boundaries to retain in integration gate:** Digest history backfills only currently persisted digests at 0007 migration, not deleted historical token values; thus a blanket all-time never-reissued assertion predating 0007 is not evidenced. SQL update guards protect ordinary mutation, **not privileged arbitrary direct SQL recreation/`INSERT OR REPLACE` of capability rows**; operator runbook must forbid such bypass and monitor privileged D1 access, while app endpoint itself uses guarded UPDATE. Lost successful replace HTTP response must not be retried; unknown bearer remains usable until intentionally replaced or revoked, so trusted generation inspection/replacement is essential. Admin trust/secret rotation/distribution/backup/restore and retention policy are NOT yet approved. Browser Origin prohibition is defense in depth, not a substitute for admin secret verification.\n\n**Disposition:** PASS restricted to implemented synthetic/local operator routes. Preserve every stacked Draft PR, repo checkpoint+recovery gates and approved ownership. No main merge, hosted Cloudflare/D1 tests, production deployment, real-alpha tokens/users, credential operations on live D1, keyring backup or Safari accepted. Next meaningful step: local release-candidate integration of the full PR440-446 stack and decision checklist for private-alpha policy; do not treat a green exact-head CI as end-to-end release approval.",
